From: bonsai-27b-fusion <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs(fusion): defect A is two things, and one has a
 demonstrated fix

GGML_CUDA_FA_ALL_QUANTS=ON corrupts attention for quantized V. Flipping it off on
this build dir, verified to have landed (cache OFF, define gone from build.ninja,
330 s rebuild instead of a no-op 26 s):

  f16K x f16V    6.9921 -> 6.9921
  f16K x q8_0V  92.5372 -> 6.9735     fixed
  q8_0K x f16V   7.3955 -> 6.9691
  q4_0K x q4_0V  7.0140 -> 7.0140
  q4_0K x q8_0V 88.6076 -> 7.0127     fixed
  q8_0K x q4_0V  7.4975 -> 6.9937
  q8_0K x q8_0V 92.2627 -> 92.2627    still broken

So most of what was reported as "q8_0 as V is broken" is a configuration defect.
That also corrects the previous entry's framing: it was true under this build's
option, not in general.

What survives is one pairing, q8_0 K x q8_0 V, broken in both configurations with
byte-identical values. Checked on it: the vec case IS declared in both branches of
the switch, dequantize_q8_0 is byte-identical to upstream, none of PrismML's 93
commits touched any FA file, and the llama.cpp base runs that pairing correctly at
both head sizes. Next step is therefore kernel level, starting at the tile kernel
where perplexity lands.

Also recorded why GGML_HIP_GRAPHS is a dead end here: it is in the CMakeCache but
appears zero times in build.ninja, so it never reached a translation unit.

Build recommendation now in state.json: keep FA_ALL_QUANTS OFF on PrismML-derived
trees. This build dir has been left that way.
