+## 2026-09-19 (final+): defect A splits in two, and one of them has a demonstrated fix
+
+Chasing defect A further. Two things happened: a build-option difference turned out
+to matter, and the "V side" framing from the previous entry turned out to be shaped
+by that option.
+
+### A1 - GGML_CUDA_FA_ALL_QUANTS=ON breaks quantized-V attention
+
+The two builds differ in 21 CMake options; the ones that can affect CUDA kernel
+selection are `GGML_CUDA_FA_ALL_QUANTS` (PrismML ON, llama.cpp fusion OFF with an
+explicit 12-combination list), `GGML_HIP_GRAPHS` (ON vs OFF) and
+`GGML_HIP_ROCWMMA_FATTN`.
+
+Flipping `GGML_CUDA_FA_ALL_QUANTS` to OFF on this worktree's build and re-running:
+
+| K | V | ON | OFF |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| f16 | f16 | 6.9921 | 6.9921 |
+| f16 | q8_0 | **92.5372** | **6.9735** |
+| q8_0 | f16 | 7.3955 | 6.9691 |
+| q4_0 | q4_0 | 7.0140 | 7.0140 |
+| q4_0 | q8_0 | 88.6076 | 7.0127 |
+| q8_0 | q4_0 | 7.4975 | 6.9937 |
+| **q8_0** | **q8_0** | **92.2627** | **92.2627** |
+
+Turning the option off fixes every quantized-V combination **except q8_0 x q8_0**.
+So the option is the single cause of most of what was being reported as "q8_0 V is
+broken", and it is a configuration defect rather than a code defect.
+
+This also **corrects the previous entry's framing**: "whenever V is q8_0 the result
+is garbage" was true *under the option that this build uses*. With the option off,
+V=q8_0 is fine with K=f16 and K=q4_0. The statement that survives is the much
+narrower one below.
+
+`GGML_HIP_GRAPHS` is a dead end in this worktree: the option is in the CMakeCache but
+**`GGML_HIP_GRAPHS` appears zero times in build.ninja**, so the define never reaches
+any translation unit - which is why flipping it produced a 26-second no-op build and
+byte-identical results. Graphs were already excluded by the runtime test
+(`GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_GRAPHS=1` -> byte-identical numbers).
+
+### A2 - q8_0 x q8_0 is broken either way
+
+The only combination that fails in both configurations, at 92.2627 with
+byte-identical per-chunk values. That is the real code defect, and its scope is now
+one pairing out of the seven measured instead of "quantized KV".
+
+Checked so far on that pairing:
+
+* the `FATTN_VEC_CASES_ALL_D(GGML_TYPE_Q8_0, GGML_TYPE_Q8_0)` case **is** declared, in
+  both branches of the `GGML_CUDA_FA_ALL_QUANTS` switch, so the chooser does find it;
+* `dequantize_q8_0` in `dequantize.cuh` is **byte-identical** to upstream's;
+* `fattn-vec.cuh`, `fattn-common.cuh`, `fattn-tile.cuh` and `fattn.cu` were not
+  touched by any of PrismML's 93 commits;
+* the llama.cpp base runs q8_0 x q8_0 correctly at both head sizes (10.7160 at 128,
+  6.9397 at 256).
+
+So the defect is in what that one kernel path depends on, and the next step is
+kernel-level rather than configuration-level: start from the tile kernel (perplexity
+exercises `BEST_FATTN_KERNEL_TILE`), comparing against upstream at the merge-base.
+
+### Method note
+
+The first attempt at the option flip "rebuilt" in 26 seconds and produced
+byte-identical numbers, which looked like "the option makes no difference". It was
+actually a **no-op**: the option was not wired into any compile command at all. The
+check that catches this is to confirm the define reached `build.ninja` (and that the
+wall clock is consistent with a real recompile - the genuine flip took 330 s). A fast
+build after a config change is a signal to verify the config actually landed, not a
+result.
+
+Second note: this build directory has `LLAMA_BUILD_TESTS=ON` from the ctest work, so a
+bare `ninja` tries to compile PrismML's `test-dspark-forward.cpp`, which does not build
+on Windows (`setenv`). Build named targets (`llama-perplexity`, `llama-server`) instead.
+
+Records: `temp_clean_later/bench-results/prism-graphs-off-build`,
+`prism-fa-allquants-off`, `prism-fusion-kv-quadrant`, `prism-graphs-probe`.
+
+### Build configuration recommendation
+
+**Do not build a PrismML-based tree with `GGML_CUDA_FA_ALL_QUANTS=ON`.** It silently
+corrupts quantized-V attention for every combination except identical quantized K and
+V. The llama.cpp fusion already builds with it OFF plus an explicit combination list,
+which is the configuration that has been behaving.
